 ## Design rule
 
-Every public analyzer is a pure function: `analyze(text: &str, options: &Options) ->
-Result<AnalysisResult>`. No analyzer touches the filesystem, the network, or shared mutable
-state across calls. This is what makes the crate embeddable in anything -- an MCP server, a
-CLI, a CI check on a manuscript repo -- without dragging along Emathy's project model,
-storage, or versioning.
+Standalone analyzers have function-specific inputs and results. The optional
+`manuscript` facade coordinates supported passes into typed findings and coverage;
+its caller-owned `AnalysisContext` bounds retained scene intermediates. Core
+analysis has no filesystem or network handling. Native model loading and the
+optional CLI are adapters. Persistence, project storage, and revision history
+belong to the caller. See [MANUSCRIPT.md](MANUSCRIPT.md) for the supported rule
+surface and conservative chronology policies.
 
